 "about": {
  "title": "About RISE",
  "sub": "Development through sports in Mayuge District, Uganda.",
  "heading": "Background and the league's logic",
  "paragraphs": [
   "The league began in 2007, started by a local organisation, Rural Urban Initiative to Support Own Efforts (RISE). It was championed early on by Kristian Bertelsen, a Danish volunteer and aspiring football coach.",
   "He started passing a new ball with a few volunteers and staff. Within 30 minutes, more than 10 young people were waiting at the sideline to join. That interest led to a tournament of eight community teams, and in November 2007 to a 14-team league with two five-month rounds a year.",
   "Many school-going youth were unemployed and had few group activities, which exposed them to isolation, risky behaviour and the HIV/AIDS wave. The league gave them a place to belong."
  ],
  "sideTitle": "How the leagues are organised",
  "sideText": "A 7-person committee: a league coordinator, four community mobilisers and two peer educators. Mobilisers are chosen democratically by the teams."
 },
